.TH CTPOOL_DECLARE_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ctpool_declare_scoped \- declare a thread pool variable with automatic RAII destruction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadpool.h>

ctpool_declare_scoped(name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Like ctpool_declare() but attaches __attribute__((cleanup(___ctpool_destroy)))
so that __ctpool_destroy() is called automatically when the variable
leaves scope.

The variable must still be assigned before use. If it is still NULL
when it goes out of scope the cleanup is a no-op.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name  Variable name to declare.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Requires GCC or Clang (uses __attribute__((cleanup))).
Perform an explicit shutdown before scope exit if drain behaviour is
important; the implicit shutdown inside __ctpool_destroy() drains the
queue, which may block for an unbounded time if tasks are long-running.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
{
    ctpool_declare_scoped(pool);
    pool = create_cthread_pool(4, 0, NULL);
    ctpool_submit(pool, my_fn, my_arg, NULL);
    ctpool_shutdown_drain(pool);
}  /* pool is destroyed automatically here */
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_declare (3),
.BR ctpool_construct_scoped (3),
.BR ___ctpool_destroy (3)
